1
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:58,440
Oh my god.

2
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:01,520
I was wondering why you were all so secretive.

3
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:02,760
You're seeing me off.

4
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:07,880
Yiran.

5
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:10,240
This poetry book is for you.

6
00:02:11,080 --> 00:02:12,680
You can flip through it when you're free.

7
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:14,640
I hope it can give you

8
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:16,520
strength and inspiration.

9
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:19,080
Thank you, Bro Min.

10
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:20,800
Good luck.

11
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:24,280
Yiran.

12
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:26,960
Uncle Chen doesn't have anything to give you,

13
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:28,680
except for a promise.

14
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,360
If you ever get bullied out there,

15
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:32,280
just let me know.

16
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:34,800
Uncle Chen will stand up for you.

17
00:02:37,280 --> 00:02:38,440
Thank you, Uncle Chen.

18
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:41,560
Yiran.

19
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:43,400
After we part today,

20
00:02:43,920 --> 00:02:46,320
who knows when we'll meet again.

21
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:47,560
The road ahead is long.

22
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:49,400
May you reach for the stars.

23
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:53,640
Actually...

24
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:55,560
Actually, I'm not going to Shanghai.

25
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:00,920
You mean...

26
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:04,240
I want to

27
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:05,560
stay at Paradise Funeral Home.

28
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:11,080
Dad!

29
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:11,680
Hold this!

30
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:15,040
Yiran,

31
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:17,240
that's a very wise decision!

32
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:19,480
The funeral industry is a blue ocean!

33
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:22,240
There are nearly 460,000 people in Lecang.

34
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:25,000
On average, 11 people pass away every day.

35
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:27,320
And with the country's aging population,

36
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:28,880
the mortality rate is rising every year.

37
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:30,360
Our business has great potential!

38
00:03:30,520 --> 00:03:30,920
Tell you what,

39
00:03:30,920 --> 00:03:32,080
I don't even need to discuss it with them,

40
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,040
I personally offer you

41
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:34,960
25% of Paradise Funeral Home's shares!

42
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:36,200
I believe with you joining us,

43
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:38,440
Paradise Funeral Home will definitely thrive!

44
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:39,320
Come on!

45
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:45,280
You joining Paradise Funeral Home

46
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:48,680
really makes Uncle Chen happy.

47
00:03:49,160 --> 00:03:51,320
I'll need your guidance from now on, Uncle Chen.

48
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:53,440
Don't mention it!

49
00:03:55,360 --> 00:03:56,440
You see,

50
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:59,040
our funeral industry

51
00:03:59,120 --> 00:04:00,480
might seem cold,

52
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:03,080
but it carries great responsibility.

53
00:04:04,200 --> 00:04:06,320
Since you chose this path,

54
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:09,640
you need to be mentally prepared.

55
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:11,200
I understand.

56
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:12,800
You have great potential.

57
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:16,200
Much better than this ungrateful son.

58
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:17,440
Exactly!

59
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:19,480
Dad,

60
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:20,600
if you don't put me down for a day,

61
00:04:20,600 --> 00:04:22,080
you just don't feel right.

62
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:23,840
If you don't talk back for a day,

63
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:24,880
you're itching for a beating!

64
00:04:26,120 --> 00:04:27,080
Alright, alright.

65
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,200
Since

66
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:29,080
Yiran is staying,

67
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:31,400
let's celebrate together!

68
00:04:31,400 --> 00:04:35,960
Welcome Li Yiran to Paradise Funeral Home!

69
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:56,640
Look at the time.

70
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:58,600
We'll miss our flight if she doesn't get back soon.

71
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:05,800
Hello.

72
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:08,000
The number you dialed is busy.

73
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:09,920
Why is the line still busy?

74
00:05:09,920 --> 00:05:10,840
Unbelievable.

75
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:17,400
Wu Huilian!

76
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:20,920
Wu Huilian!

77
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:24,080
Wu Huilian!

78
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:29,320
Wu Huilian!

79
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,520
Why are you staring at me?

80
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:35,600
Hurry up and come move this!

81
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:36,680
We're going to miss our flight!

82
00:05:36,680 --> 00:05:37,400
Do you know what time it is?

83
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:38,960
Wu Huilian!

84
00:05:41,200 --> 00:05:42,000
And you are...?

85
00:05:42,200 --> 00:05:43,080
Why are you yelling at me?

86
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:44,480
I'm telling you to get up here and move things!

87
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:45,840
I'm not leaving.

88
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:50,080
Say that again.

89
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,320
I'm not leaving.

90
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,600
I'm not going back to Shanghai.

91
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:09,640
Yiran!

92
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:10,560
Is this for real?

93
00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:11,960
You can't joke about this.

94
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,600
Don't get your mom's hopes up for nothing.

95
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:19,960
Yiran,

96
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:20,840
you're not lying to us, are you?

97
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:51,160
Really?

98
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:54,920
I'm not leaving.

99
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:00,840
Why aren't you leaving?

100
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:02,200
Didn't you say you were leaving?

101
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:03,680
You want me to leave?

102
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:04,200
Fine.

103
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:05,040
I can leave.

104
00:07:05,280 --> 00:07:06,080
I didn't say that.

105
00:07:08,080 --> 00:07:10,080
You...

106
00:07:10,080 --> 00:07:11,000
Are you leaving or not?

107
00:07:11,840 --> 00:07:12,920
I'm not leaving.

108
00:07:12,920 --> 00:07:14,000
Not leaving, not leaving.

109
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:15,400
If she's not leaving, then she's not leaving.

110
00:07:15,400 --> 00:07:16,400
Why are you yelling?

111
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:20,840
What do you want for lunch today?

112
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:21,760
I'll cook for you.

113
00:07:21,880 --> 00:07:22,520
Da Ren.

114
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:23,400
Let's eat together.

115
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:24,000
Okay, okay.

116
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:24,800
Sounds good.

117
00:07:24,960 --> 00:07:25,800
Yiran.

118
00:07:25,800 --> 00:07:27,400
Look how happy your mom is.

119
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:29,200
Yiran.

120
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:30,720
I'm just glad you're staying.

121
00:07:34,160 --> 00:07:36,280
Sister Yiran isn't leaving!

122
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,240
Give it to me.

123
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:57,960
I'll take the front.

124
00:07:58,760 --> 00:07:59,640
Heavy, heavy, heavy!

125
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:11,400
Where are Uncle Da Ren and the rest?

126
00:08:13,200 --> 00:08:15,480
They said they're not eating with us.

127
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:18,560
So we can enjoy some alone time together.

128
00:08:23,600 --> 00:08:24,400
You...

129
00:08:25,920 --> 00:08:27,360
just decided not to leave like that.

130
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:29,800
Couldn't bear to part with me, could you?

131
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:31,120
I have to say,

132
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:31,800
Wu Huilian,

133
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,360
the hotpot you make...

134
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:34,600
is truly unbeatable.

135
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:36,400
Keep changing the subject, why don't you.

136
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,800
You won't get this taste in Shanghai anyway.

137
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:41,360
Have some more of that free-range chicken.

138
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:43,600
You've loved it since you were little.

139
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:46,040
You used to finish a whole chicken by yourself.

140
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:51,120
It's delicious.

141
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:52,200
Still tastes exactly the same.

142
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:54,760
But such a good job...

143
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:57,360
and you just gave it up like that.

144
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:01,600
Didn't I write you a guarantee?

145
00:09:01,960 --> 00:09:04,000
I said I wouldn't lose my job again.

146
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:05,400
Those guarantees you write...

147
00:09:05,400 --> 00:09:06,360
when have they ever worked?

148
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:09,480
I'm staying, and you're still not happy.

149
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:10,800
Yiran,

150
00:09:12,600 --> 00:09:13,520
honestly,

151
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:16,520
good opportunities in life are rare.

152
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,760
Being able to go to a big city like Shanghai

153
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:21,040
and find a good job

154
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:23,200
is an especially rare chance.

155
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:25,520
Look at this small town of ours.

156
00:09:25,840 --> 00:09:27,200
So many young people

157
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:28,760
do whatever it takes

158
00:09:28,760 --> 00:09:30,360
to make it in the big city.

159
00:09:30,800 --> 00:09:32,080
I'm afraid you'll regret it.

160
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:34,320
How do you know

161
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,880
I'll definitely regret staying?

162
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:45,360
Come on,

163
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:46,200
let's have a drink.

164
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:49,640
Welcome back.

165
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:51,880
No, wait.

166
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:54,000
Congratulations.

167
00:09:56,240 --> 00:09:57,880
Not that either. I should...

168
00:09:58,080 --> 00:09:58,880
Let's just have a drink.

169
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:00,760
Come on, let's drink.

170
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:07,960
I'm allowed to drink today, right?

171
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:09,600
Just this one glass.

172
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:10,880
Alright.

173
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:20,600
Have some more. Eat up.

174
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:21,880
I'm full.

175
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:25,760
Take your time.

176
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:30,400
I'm heading downstairs.

177
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:34,120
Yiran.

178
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:35,760
Are you really...

179
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:37,320
I said I'm not leaving,

180
00:10:37,320 --> 00:10:38,600
and I really mean it.

181
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:40,800
Wild horses couldn't drag me away.

182
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:25,120
Lao Li.

183
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,040
Did you hear that?

184
00:11:27,800 --> 00:11:29,440
Yiran said she's not leaving.

185
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:32,240
She's staying to keep me company.

186
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:35,240
I'm so happy.

187
00:11:36,920 --> 00:11:38,440
Here.

188
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:39,600
Have a drink too.

189
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:42,000
Didn't you say,

190
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:44,920
drink celebratory wine every day,

191
00:11:46,040 --> 00:11:47,480
and happy events will come your way?

192
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:49,200
Drink up.

193
00:11:54,240 --> 00:12:00,200
You ask how deep my love for you is,

194
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:06,160
how much I love you.

195
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:08,960
Your feelings are true.

196
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:17,400
Dear listeners,

197
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:19,400
welcome to the Voice of Lecang.

198
00:12:19,560 --> 00:12:21,600
Today marks the Beginning of Autumn,

199
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:24,200
the thirteenth of the twenty-four solar terms,

200
00:12:24,400 --> 00:12:26,080
and the start of the autumn season.

201
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:27,760
Starting from today,

202
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:29,400
we officially enter autumn.

203
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:31,360
Have you all felt

204
00:12:31,360 --> 00:12:33,400
the joy of the approaching autumn?

205
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:36,000
Autumn means harvest.

206
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:37,240
Actually,

207
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:40,720
I'm not planning to go to Shanghai anymore.

208
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:45,000
I want to stay at Paradise Funeral Home.

209
00:13:06,520 --> 00:13:07,320
Director.

210
00:13:07,760 --> 00:13:08,480
I mostly

211
00:13:08,480 --> 00:13:09,400
wanted to talk to you again

212
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:11,160
about the returning youth project.

213
00:13:11,160 --> 00:13:13,240
Wasn't that project already axed?

214
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,480
But I've been on this project for quite a while.

215
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:18,680
Just because you've been on it a while,

216
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:20,000
does it mean you have to keep going?

217
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,960
You young folks need to learn to cut your losses.

218
00:13:22,480 --> 00:13:23,280
Director,

219
00:13:23,440 --> 00:13:25,000
please see what else you can do.

220
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:26,720
This project, to me,

221
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:27,640
is really important.

222
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:28,600
Shiqi,

223
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:32,040
if it weren't for your dad,

224
00:13:32,120 --> 00:13:34,040
I wouldn't have approved this project.

225
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:36,200
You saw the Deputy Director's attitude.

226
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:38,800
This is my job.

227
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:40,400
What does my dad have to do with it?

228
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:42,560
In that case,

229
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:44,120
let me tell you the truth.

230
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,640
Stop wasting your effort on this project.

231
00:13:48,920 --> 00:13:49,640
What do you mean?

232
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:50,560
It means,

233
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:53,120
because your dad brings the station ad revenue,

234
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:56,200
everyone does him a favor.

235
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:57,360
Got it?

236
00:14:09,040 --> 00:14:10,160
Yiran.

237
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:12,360
Are you really coming to work tomorrow?

238
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:14,840
Chen Xiaofang,

239
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:16,200
do you regret giving me shares?

240
00:14:16,200 --> 00:14:17,360
Of course not!

241
00:14:18,960 --> 00:14:20,360
Trust my judgment.

242
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:22,560
We have an aging population now.

243
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:24,120
The silver economy is definitely the next big thing.

244
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:25,800
Okay, okay.

245
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:27,360
Enough with your business talk.

246
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:31,520
Let me tell you, Yiran.

247
00:14:31,680 --> 00:14:33,800
I'm not the only one happy you're staying.

248
00:14:34,440 --> 00:14:35,960
Someone else is even happier.

249
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:36,760
Right?

250
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:43,560
I am not!

251
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:44,600
Stop talking nonsense.

252
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:46,000
I didn't even say who it was.

253
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,040
Why are you getting so worked up?

254
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:49,520
I'm telling you,

255
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:51,920
this morning, he was working

256
00:14:51,920 --> 00:14:53,280
with so much energy.

257
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:54,600
He even kept singing.

258
00:14:57,560 --> 00:14:58,240
What?

259
00:15:09,400 --> 00:15:10,560
Li Yiran

260
00:15:10,560 --> 00:15:11,640
You're really not leaving?

261
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:13,920
I'm not leaving.

262
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:15,800
I plan to stay and work here.

263
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:19,840
Congratulations then.

264
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:22,280
Thanks.

265
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:24,560
I'm heading home.

266
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:25,320
I'll walk you.

267
00:15:26,520 --> 00:15:27,240
Let's go.

268
00:15:32,160 --> 00:15:34,520
Xiaofang, you're the most generous!

269
00:15:34,520 --> 00:15:35,480
You're not Xiaofang.

270
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:36,440
You're Dafang.

271
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:39,640
Chen Dafang, wait for me!

272
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:53,880
If the station says no, just let it go.

273
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:57,000
You've already done your best.

274
00:16:05,160 --> 00:16:08,320
So even you think...

275
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:11,720
...I should just drop it if they won't let me film?

276
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:14,160
No.

277
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:15,480
I... I didn't mean it like that.

278
00:16:15,480 --> 00:16:16,160
Shiqi.

279
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:17,040
I mean...

280
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:19,800
...in my personal experience,

281
00:16:20,160 --> 00:16:21,280
sometimes you just have to

282
00:16:21,280 --> 00:16:23,400
do things you don't want to do, and then

283
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:25,520
you'll get the chance to do what you want.

284
00:16:48,840 --> 00:16:49,800
You're drunk.

285
00:16:49,800 --> 00:16:51,080
Chen Baixi.

286
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:53,520
You'll never know

287
00:16:53,520 --> 00:16:54,840
just to get close to you,

288
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:58,840
how hard those hundred steps were.

289
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:03,200
But I don't care.

290
00:17:03,440 --> 00:17:04,640
What I care about is that

291
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:08,800
when I've given it my absolute all

292
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:10,080
to fight against the whole world,

293
00:17:10,080 --> 00:17:11,680
you turn around and tell me

294
00:17:11,680 --> 00:17:13,040
to forget it if we can't shoot.

295
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,160
Why should I forget it?

296
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:18,320
Just because everyone only respects my dad

297
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:20,320
enough to give me a chance?

298
00:17:21,840 --> 00:17:22,720
Then what about me?

299
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:26,560
What am I?

300
00:17:31,880 --> 00:17:33,000
Is my life

301
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:35,120
just doomed

302
00:17:35,120 --> 00:17:38,400
to follow everyone else's plans and expectations?

303
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:44,040
When you say that,

304
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:48,200
you make me feel like my life is a joke.

305
00:17:50,760 --> 00:17:52,400
A joke completely at the mercy of others.

306
00:17:57,880 --> 00:17:58,600
You're drunk.

307
00:17:58,600 --> 00:17:59,800
Let me take you home.

308
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:01,040
I'm not drunk.

309
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:03,280
I'm more sober now than I've ever been.

310
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:09,320
Chen Baixi.

311
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:12,880
You like Li Yiran,

312
00:18:13,320 --> 00:18:14,280
right?

313
00:18:25,320 --> 00:18:26,440
You don't have to answer.

314
00:18:28,920 --> 00:18:30,080
I know the answer.

315
00:19:01,800 --> 00:19:02,480
Checkmate.

316
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:09,440
Since you're staying, settle in.

317
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:12,320
Starting today,

318
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:13,600
no more infighting.

319
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:16,120
For a better life for the people,

320
00:19:16,120 --> 00:19:16,800
we must strive.

321
00:19:20,240 --> 00:19:21,120
Let's go!

322
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:23,560
Morning!

323
00:19:23,560 --> 00:19:24,360
Jeez!

324
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:25,840
Morning.

325
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:26,960
Morning.

326
00:19:27,360 --> 00:19:27,960
Morning, Uncle.

327
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:31,680
Lifeless young people,

328
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:34,680
vibrant seniors.

329
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:35,800
Ermao.

330
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:37,480
Bye.

331
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:38,760
I'm off to work.

332
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:40,280
Take care, take care.

333
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:44,080
Seeing a ghost first thing in the morning.

334
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:47,440
What are you looking at?

335
00:19:47,720 --> 00:19:48,920
I'll stew you into soup for my mom.

336
00:20:07,440 --> 00:20:09,000
Colleagues,

337
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:10,160
look alive.

338
00:20:11,440 --> 00:20:12,240
Let's start the meeting.

339
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:13,360
First of all,

340
00:20:13,360 --> 00:20:15,000
let's introduce the new member of our department.

341
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:17,120
You might have bumped into her before.

342
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:18,840
Go ahead and introduce yourself.

343
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:23,600
Hello everyone, I'm Wu Huilian.

344
00:20:24,320 --> 00:20:26,200
I just became the new dating consultant.

345
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:27,320
I look forward to working with you.

346
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:29,040
Let's welcome her.

347
00:20:30,920 --> 00:20:31,600
Show some enthusiasm.

348
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:32,480
Welcome!

349
00:20:38,280 --> 00:20:39,320
New members,

350
00:20:39,320 --> 00:20:40,360
new journey.

351
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:43,400
Paradise Funeral Home needs a fresh look too.

352
00:20:44,400 --> 00:20:45,600
Fortune-telling matchmaking,

353
00:20:45,600 --> 00:20:47,000
face and palm reading,

354
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,400
marrying within the extended family...

355
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:49,800
All that outdated stuff?

356
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:51,120
We're ditching it all!

357
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:55,080
Joy Bells must keep up with the latest trends.

358
00:20:55,320 --> 00:20:56,280
Zodiac sign matching

359
00:20:56,280 --> 00:20:57,280
and the 16 Personality Types Test

360
00:20:57,280 --> 00:21:00,640
are what's popular with young people today.

361
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:01,920
What kind of freak?

362
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:06,400
As for the middle-aged and elderly,

363
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:08,240
it's fine if they don't get the 16 Personality Types Test.

364
00:21:08,680 --> 00:21:11,920
We'll create an exclusive Joy Bells version.

365
00:21:12,120 --> 00:21:14,240
Like the Square Dance Leader Personality,

366
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,800
Wellness & Lying Flat Personality,

367
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:18,160
Family-Oriented Personality,

368
00:21:18,160 --> 00:21:20,960
and Generous Pension Personality.

369
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:22,920
We have it all.

370
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:24,400
With Yiran joining us,

371
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:27,040
Paradise Funeral Home is now a limited liability company.

372
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:29,680
So, we need to change our business strategy.

373
00:21:29,680 --> 00:21:31,560
We can't just wait for business to come to us.

374
00:21:31,560 --> 00:21:33,600
We have to take the initiative.

375
00:21:34,280 --> 00:21:36,240
Are we going to hand out flyers in neighborhoods?

376
00:21:36,240 --> 00:21:37,440
Or wait around at hospitals?

377
00:21:37,440 --> 00:21:38,120
No, no, no.

378
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:41,400
We're going fully digital and smart.

379
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:46,760
The three-kilometer radius around a hospital is a prime location.

380
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:49,840
Oncology and inpatient wards are our VIP client pool.

381
00:21:49,840 --> 00:21:52,920
The ICU is our precise customer profiling zone.

382
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:56,840
Combine that with census data on the local elderly,

383
00:21:56,840 --> 00:21:59,400
and enter it all into our computer system.

384
00:22:00,720 --> 00:22:01,520
Xiaofang...

385
00:22:02,400 --> 00:22:03,920
Why do I feel like this is a bit unethical?

386
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:05,400
Amitabha.

387
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:06,400
No, no, no.

388
00:22:07,080 --> 00:22:07,840
Today,

389
00:22:07,880 --> 00:22:10,920
I'm going to correct your flawed way of thinking.

390
00:22:10,920 --> 00:22:13,240
The rising divorce rate today

391
00:22:13,640 --> 00:22:17,880
is both an opportunity and a challenge for us.

392
00:22:18,280 --> 00:22:19,320
Look at it from a positive angle.

393
00:22:20,080 --> 00:22:21,280
With more people getting divorced,

394
00:22:21,400 --> 00:22:24,280
the middle-aged and elderly market naturally booms.

395
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:27,000
So, for Joy Bells,

396
00:22:27,040 --> 00:22:28,920
opening up a new track

397
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:30,240
is absolutely urgent.

398
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:33,000
Taking the initiative doesn't mean we're wishing for people to die.

399
00:22:33,160 --> 00:22:33,920
We're doing this

400
00:22:33,920 --> 00:22:37,000
to provide timely, precise, and efficient service to those in need.

401
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:37,920
What is

402
00:22:37,920 --> 00:22:38,720
our slogan?

403
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:41,600
Full of joy and happiness,

404
00:22:42,400 --> 00:22:44,080
get married with Joy Bells!

405
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:47,120
Our goal is:

406
00:22:47,640 --> 00:22:49,240
Pre-plan your afterlife services while alive,

407
00:22:49,240 --> 00:22:50,720
personalized farewell ceremonies,

408
00:22:50,720 --> 00:22:52,240
and chain-store value-added services!

409
00:22:52,720 --> 00:22:53,520
Next,

410
00:22:53,640 --> 00:22:57,600
we'll play matchmaker for all the men and women in Lecang.

411
00:22:58,120 --> 00:22:59,520
Let the dead rest in peace,

412
00:22:59,520 --> 00:23:00,960
and give the living peace of mind.

413
00:23:00,960 --> 00:23:02,600
We need to achieve standardization,

414
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:03,240
scalability,

415
00:23:03,240 --> 00:23:04,440
and ultimately, globalization!

416
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:06,800
Let's work together,

417
00:23:06,800 --> 00:23:08,000
make it bigger and stronger,

418
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:09,400
and create brilliance together!

419
00:23:09,600 --> 00:23:10,760
Applaud if you understand!

420
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:26,960
Mr. Wang! Mr. Wang!

421
00:23:27,800 --> 00:23:28,440
Don't worry.

422
00:23:28,440 --> 00:23:29,920
That diamond urn for your dad

423
00:23:29,920 --> 00:23:31,240
is absolutely Hearts and Arrows.

424
00:23:31,240 --> 00:23:33,200
It's super high-end and classy.

425
00:23:35,120 --> 00:23:35,880
What are you guys doing?

426
00:23:35,880 --> 00:23:37,120
I wasn't finished speaking yet.

427
00:23:38,200 --> 00:23:39,280
Sorry, Mr. Wang.

428
00:23:39,400 --> 00:23:40,200
Please continue.

429
00:23:40,200 --> 00:23:41,240
Did everyone get that?

430
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:42,240
Got it.

431
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:43,800
Meeting adjourned. Get to work.

432
00:23:50,080 --> 00:23:50,800
How did the recording turn out?

433
00:23:50,800 --> 00:23:53,600
Don't worry, absolute career man vibes.

434
00:23:54,280 --> 00:23:55,080
Okay.

435
00:23:55,760 --> 00:23:57,360
Send a copy of this video to my dad.

436
00:23:58,000 --> 00:23:58,680
As for me,

437
00:23:58,680 --> 00:23:59,800
I'll post it on my Moments too.

438
00:24:00,680 --> 00:24:02,200
I want Xiaofang to see.

439
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:04,600
A man focused on his career

440
00:24:06,240 --> 00:24:07,480
is the most charming.

441
00:24:08,480 --> 00:24:09,960
So charming.

442
00:24:17,400 --> 00:24:17,880
Hurry up!

443
00:24:17,880 --> 00:24:19,040
You can't catch me!

444
00:24:19,200 --> 00:24:20,000
I almost got it!

445
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:20,640
You can't catch me!

446
00:24:20,640 --> 00:24:21,680
Daddy, don't run!

447
00:24:23,120 --> 00:24:24,040
How did you catch it before me?

448
00:24:24,040 --> 00:24:25,160
Sweetie.

449
00:24:25,520 --> 00:24:26,400
Is it fun?

450
00:24:28,480 --> 00:24:29,400
You're not leaving?

451
00:24:29,720 --> 00:24:30,840
Xiaofang is really happy.

452
00:24:32,480 --> 00:24:33,920
Is she the only one who's happy?

453
00:24:36,200 --> 00:24:36,680
We...

454
00:24:36,680 --> 00:24:37,760
We're all very happy.

455
00:24:39,360 --> 00:24:40,480
Can't catch it!

456
00:24:44,760 --> 00:24:48,000
When I first came back, I wasn't used to it either.

457
00:24:48,920 --> 00:24:52,120
But now, it feels pretty good.

458
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:56,000
Yeah.

459
00:24:57,760 --> 00:24:59,520
Back when I was in Shanghai,

460
00:24:59,520 --> 00:25:02,640
I had to squeeze on the subway, order takeout,

461
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:06,200
work overtime, and catch the last train.

462
00:25:08,600 --> 00:25:10,760
Life gave me no time to even catch my breath.

463
00:25:11,960 --> 00:25:13,800
Not only did I not make much money,

464
00:25:14,640 --> 00:25:16,400
my temper got worse too.

465
00:25:21,960 --> 00:25:23,120
Bro Min was right.

466
00:25:24,920 --> 00:25:27,240
Not everyone has to achieve great things.

467
00:25:28,040 --> 00:25:29,920
Life is meant to be experienced.

468
00:25:31,400 --> 00:25:32,200
So,

469
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:35,040
I've decided to fully experience my life now.

470
00:25:39,120 --> 00:25:41,120
Is that your reason for staying?

471
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:04,400
Maybe

472
00:26:06,200 --> 00:26:08,480
the evening breeze here

473
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:11,000
understands me better than Lujiazui's neon lights.

474
00:26:18,320 --> 00:26:20,080
Don't you think so,

475
00:26:20,080 --> 00:26:21,120
Chen Baixi?

476
00:26:28,040 --> 00:26:29,080
The evening breeze tells me

477
00:26:30,640 --> 00:26:31,760
yes.

478
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:11,040
Why did you come in with your outside shoes on?

479
00:27:11,040 --> 00:27:11,840
Go change your shoes.

480
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:13,800
I can't walk anymore.

481
00:27:13,800 --> 00:27:14,640
I'm freaking exhausted.

482
00:27:25,960 --> 00:27:27,680
I thought

483
00:27:27,680 --> 00:27:30,200
getting a job would be pretty relaxing.

484
00:27:30,600 --> 00:27:32,640
But that bastard Zhou Fang

485
00:27:32,640 --> 00:27:34,200
fed us pipe dreams all day.

486
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:36,520
Talked so much.

487
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:38,720
The worst part is I didn't understand a word.

488
00:27:38,800 --> 00:27:40,480
Whose fault is that?

489
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:42,320
That's just how society is now.

490
00:27:42,320 --> 00:27:43,520
You're never too old to learn.

491
00:27:44,960 --> 00:27:46,640
Crying at funerals is way more straightforward.

492
00:27:46,640 --> 00:27:48,160
My head hurts so much from studying.

493
00:27:48,200 --> 00:27:49,600
Even my heart aches now.

494
00:27:50,560 --> 00:27:52,480
All roads lead to being a corporate slave.

495
00:27:52,640 --> 00:27:55,360
Now you see the hell us wage slaves go through.

496
00:27:56,800 --> 00:27:58,000
Lying flat is so comfortable.

497
00:27:58,440 --> 00:27:59,800
Why bother grinding?

498
00:27:59,800 --> 00:28:01,240
Grind, my ass.

499
00:28:01,800 --> 00:28:03,040
Everyone is grinding.

500
00:28:05,560 --> 00:28:06,840
You need to have perseverance.

501
00:28:06,840 --> 00:28:08,200
You need to stay focused.

502
00:28:08,400 --> 00:28:09,800
Adding things is human nature.

503
00:28:09,800 --> 00:28:12,040
Subtracting is true wisdom.

504
00:28:12,320 --> 00:28:13,120
Wait right here.

505
00:28:14,440 --> 00:28:15,800
I don't have any wisdom.

506
00:28:16,040 --> 00:28:17,400
Right now, I'm just sleepy.

507
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:28,000
I picked out a few simple books for you.

508
00:28:28,000 --> 00:28:28,960
You can read these first.

509
00:28:30,400 --> 00:28:31,200
Wake up.

510
00:28:32,760 --> 00:28:33,680
Wake up.

511
00:28:33,680 --> 00:28:34,840
It's only been a few minutes.

512
00:28:34,840 --> 00:28:35,920
And you're already asleep.

513
00:28:36,600 --> 00:28:37,120
Here.

514
00:28:37,600 --> 00:28:38,800
These are pretty simple.

515
00:28:38,800 --> 00:28:39,640
What are you doing?

516
00:28:39,640 --> 00:28:40,640
Bringing all these books.

517
00:28:41,600 --> 00:28:43,800
Presentations, spreadsheets...

518
00:28:43,800 --> 00:28:45,280
This is a word processor. Learn this first.

519
00:28:47,800 --> 00:28:48,600
Word?

520
00:28:50,320 --> 00:28:51,640
I'm actually a bit hungry now.

521
00:28:52,320 --> 00:28:53,520
What's for dinner tonight?

522
00:28:54,920 --> 00:28:56,600
Stop changing the subject.

523
00:28:56,760 --> 00:28:58,280
Read this book before dinner.

524
00:28:58,280 --> 00:28:58,800
It's just a little bit.

525
00:28:58,800 --> 00:28:59,600
It'll be quick.

526
00:28:59,600 --> 00:29:00,640
No dinner until you finish it.

527
00:29:02,400 --> 00:29:03,640
Like I don't know how to cook.

528
00:29:04,240 --> 00:29:05,520
You're not allowed to cook.

529
00:29:05,760 --> 00:29:06,720
I can make instant noodles.

530
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:08,200
No instant noodles either.

531
00:29:09,520 --> 00:29:10,520
And no ordering takeout.

532
00:29:10,640 --> 00:29:11,520
I'll check on you later.

533
00:29:13,240 --> 00:29:14,360
Why are you being so fierce?

534
00:29:23,160 --> 00:29:24,880
What is this stuff?

535
00:29:46,640 --> 00:29:47,880
These videos, you...

536
00:29:49,280 --> 00:29:50,480
You fall asleep as soon as you read.

537
00:29:50,760 --> 00:29:51,680
What kind of attitude is this?

538
00:29:51,680 --> 00:29:52,840
Are you learning this for me?

539
00:29:52,960 --> 00:29:54,200
Why are you yelling?

540
00:29:55,600 --> 00:29:56,600
What kind of book is this?

541
00:29:56,600 --> 00:29:57,560
Look at it yourself.

542
00:29:57,560 --> 00:29:58,840
It's full of boxes.

543
00:29:59,040 --> 00:30:00,000
Looks like chicken scratch.

544
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:00,680
I've read it.

545
00:30:00,680 --> 00:30:01,640
This is the one I read.

546
00:30:01,640 --> 00:30:02,480
What's so hard to understand?

547
00:30:02,480 --> 00:30:03,440
They're all Chinese characters.

548
00:30:04,800 --> 00:30:06,840
I've hated reading since I was a kid.

549
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:09,000
As soon as I read, I fall asleep.

550
00:30:15,440 --> 00:30:16,400
You don't like reading, huh?

551
00:30:16,400 --> 00:30:17,040
Fine.

552
00:30:17,760 --> 00:30:18,640
Take online classes then.

553
00:30:18,840 --> 00:30:20,160
I found some tutorial videos for you.

554
00:30:20,160 --> 00:30:21,680
They're online. Watch them.

555
00:30:22,280 --> 00:30:23,680
I don't like online classes.

556
00:30:25,960 --> 00:30:27,000
If you watch them,

557
00:30:27,480 --> 00:30:29,000
I'll do all the chores this month.

558
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:32,960
Really?

559
00:30:33,680 --> 00:30:34,800
Laundry, cooking,

560
00:30:34,880 --> 00:30:36,160
cleaning,

561
00:30:36,160 --> 00:30:36,880
scrubbing the toilet,

562
00:30:36,880 --> 00:30:37,680
you'll do it all?

563
00:30:39,080 --> 00:30:40,840
I probably can't finish in a month.

564
00:30:41,680 --> 00:30:42,480
A month and a half.

565
00:30:43,800 --> 00:30:44,600
Two months.

566
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:45,880
Two months it is.

567
00:30:45,880 --> 00:30:47,400
It's a deal. Let's start now.

568
00:30:47,400 --> 00:30:47,960
Come on.

569
00:30:51,560 --> 00:30:52,280
Come here.

570
00:30:52,880 --> 00:30:53,760
I'm coming.

571
00:30:53,760 --> 00:30:54,880
No need to be so fierce.

572
00:30:56,760 --> 00:30:57,560
Watch closely.

573
00:30:58,160 --> 00:30:59,680
This is the power button.

574
00:30:59,680 --> 00:31:00,880
Press it to turn it on.

575
00:31:03,600 --> 00:31:04,680
Press it. What are you waiting for?

576
00:31:04,680 --> 00:31:05,880
Waiting for me to press it?

